  "notes": [
    "A r=1: no reply within 1500 ms",
    "path byte lengths are counted on the path without the leading slash, segments joined by \"/\", UTF-8 bytes (all ASCII here): 812 (two 400-char segments under golden/len), 769, 768; the put value d is that byte count.",
    "(d2) /golden/len/<759 x> has segment bytes 6+3+759 = 768 (770 joined with \"/\"); /golden/len/<760 y> has 769 (771 joined).",
    "A r=13: no reply within 1500 ms",
    "A r=14: no reply within 1500 ms",
    "A r=18: no reply within 1500 ms",
    "data-path cases: /g {a:{<765>}} (keys inside data joined \"a/<765>\" = 767 bytes), /g {ab:{<765>}} (768 bytes); /gg {<766>} (segment-byte sum path+key = 2+766 = 768), /gg {<767>} (769).",
    "key-length cases:keys of 766, 767, 768 and 769 bytes in data under /golden/limits/k<len>, then keys of 765 and 766 bytes under /gk, i.e. full path gk/<key> of exactly 768 and 769 bytes.",
    "A r=25: no reply within 1500 ms",
    "A r=29: no reply within 1500 ms",
    "nesting cases: put at /golden/deep/l<N> (3 path segments) of {\"k\":{\"k\":...1}} with N nested objects, N in 29..33; then put at /gdeep (1 path segment) with N in 30..33. Each data leaf sits at depth (path segments + N).",
    "(g) chunked put: message of 60061 chars sent as count frame + 4 chunks of <= 16384 chars.",
    "A r=31: no reply within 1500 ms (connection closed)",
    "(h) single unsplit text frame of 120062 chars.",
    "Frames longer than 1000 chars are stored as {len, sha256} (sha256 of the UTF-8 frame text).",
    "Observed with firebase-database-emulator-v4.11.2: forbidden char in a data key -> t:\"e\" control frame, no reply. Forbidden char in path -> invalid_parameters \"Invalid token in path\". Depth: path segments + data nesting must be <= 32 (31 and 32 segment paths pass, 33 fails) else invalid_parameters \"Path specified exceeds the maximum depth that can be written (32).\"; a value nested >= 33 objects deep inside d fails earlier with the t:\"e\" frame. Length: the sum of UTF-8 bytes of all segments (path + keys inside d), separators not counted, must be <= 768 else invalid_parameters \"Path specified exceeds the maximum length that can be written (768 bytes).\"; independently, keys inside d joined with \"/\" must be < 768 bytes, else the t:\"e\" frame. A count-prefixed chunked 60 KB message is accepted and pushed to the listener in 16384-char chunks with a count frame; a single unsplit ~120 KB text frame makes the server close the socket with 1002.",
    "close initiated by the client (close frame with code 1000) on: B; the code recorded is what the client saw in the emulator's closing reply (1005 = the reply carried no status code).",
    "close initiated by the server on: A."
  ]
